# Copy to `.dev.vars` (gitignored) for `vp run backend#dev` (wrangler dev). Only real secrets go
# here — GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID/TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY/TURNSTILE_HOSTNAMES are set in wrangler.jsonc's
# `vars` (see wrangler.jsonc.example), since they're not secrets, just don't reuse the original
# author's own OAuth client / Turnstile widget.

# Optional — a random value keeps sessions alive across `wrangler dev` restarts.
# SESSION_SECRET=

# Required for `wrangler dev` (worker.ts always calls the real Turnstile siteverify — unlike the
# Node entrypoint's stub) — the secret half of your own Turnstile widget from wrangler.jsonc's
# TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY.
# TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY=

# Optional but needed to actually create a Transfer Session locally — overrides wrangler.jsonc's
# TURNSTILE_HOSTNAMES (which only lists the production hostname). Without this, siteverify's
# `hostname` comes back as `localhost` and never matches, so Turnstile verification 403s on every
# attempt even though the widget itself solves successfully.
# TURNSTILE_HOSTNAMES=localhost
